  "sourceUrl": "https://anaisninfoundation.org/diaries",
  "en": [
   "Anaïs Nin's diary began reaching public readers in edited volumes in 1966. Yet the printed books did not include everything she had written in her private journals.",
   "Diary writing occupies an unstable place between private life and literature. A passage can tell the truth of the moment without having been written for the strangers who later encounter it.",
   "The original series was edited. Later unexpurgated volumes, published beginning in 1986, restored material about relationships and intimate life omitted from the earlier versions.",
   "Editing a diary can protect living people, control a literary persona or reflect personal judgment. We should not assume that every omission had one shared purpose.",
   "The foundation records the different publication series. Their dates and editorial histories show the gap between a diary existing and a particular version of it becoming public.",
   "Readers now face several versions of the same life. Rather than calling one a simple lie, the archive invites scrutiny of who decided which pages entered the public record and when."
  ],
  "zh": [
   "1966年，阿娜伊丝·宁的日记开始以书籍形式进入读者视野。然而，公众读到的并不是她曾经写下的全部文字。部分私人关系与情感经历被删去，留在公开版本之外。",
   "日记处于私人生活与文学之间。写日记时，一个人未必始终想象未来会有多少陌生人阅读自己的文字；真正出版时，却不得不重新决定谁可以进入那些原本亲密的篇章。",
   "最初公开的是经过编辑的日记系列。从1986年开始，更接近原貌的未删节卷册陆续出版，使此前未出现的内容重新进入读者视野。",
   "删节可能关系到对亲友的保护、作者形象以及个人判断，但我们不能把所有删除都看作同一种谎言，也不能忽略编辑者和出版者在不同年代发挥的作用。",
   "阿娜伊丝·宁基金会记录了日记不同系列的出版时间及内容差异。对比版本能证明文字曾被保留，却不能让我们轻易判断每处删节背后的全部心意。",
   "今天，读者面对的是同一人生的不同公开版本。所谓完整与不完整，不只是一本书的厚度，更涉及一个写作者是否能决定让世界在什么时间知道多少。"
  ],
  "zhQuestion": "日记一旦出版，作者是否就必须交出所有曾经写下的私人生活？",
